# Chapter 10 — Database & API Design (MVP)

## Database

No database is required for the initial version.

All business content is stored in structured TypeScript configuration files.

Future migration to PostgreSQL or Supabase should be straightforward.

---

## API Endpoints

### POST /api/contact

Accepts contact form submissions.

Returns:

* Success status
* Confirmation message

---

### POST /api/quote

Accepts quote requests.

Triggers email notification to the agency.

---

### POST /api/newsletter

Reserved for future newsletter functionality.

---

## Data Validation

* Required field checks
* Email format validation
* Phone format validation
* Spam protection
* Server-side validation before processing

